summary:
  Where a device plays alone, a notch of the wheel counts from the level
  the output here stands at.

history:
  Nothing that starts on a device alone touches the output here. After
  the wake-up alarm told a device 40 %, it still stood at last night's
  80 %, and one notch down sent the device from 0.200 to 0.375.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      if (away === true && Number.isFinite(own)) base = own;

replace:
      if (away === true && Number.isFinite(own)) base = base;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_where_a_device_plays_alone_a_notch_counts_from_the_listeners_level
  and tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_after_an_alarm_on_a_device_that_plays_alone_a_notch_counts_from_the_alarms_level.
  Line-neutral.
